From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 23:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: expand PPE direct-switch TX pool

Match the QSDK default direct-switch TX descriptor count.  The PPE WBM
completion ring already contains 32768 entries, but a pool of only 8192
descriptors can starve PPE2TCL well before the completion ring reaches its
designed capacity under high-rate downlink traffic.

The cookie format provides 11 page bits and each SPT page contains 512
entries, so the resulting 64 pages remain within the hardware encoding.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.h
@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@ struct ath12k_pdev_dp {
 #define DP_PPE2TCL_RING_SIZE		8192
 #define DP_REO2PPE_RING_SIZE		16384
 #define DP_PPE_WBM2SW_RING_SIZE		32768
-#define DP_PPE_DS_TX_DESC_COUNT		8192
+#define DP_PPE_DS_TX_DESC_COUNT		32768
 #define HAL_REO2PPE_DST_IND		6
 #define DP_PPE_DS_TX_SPT_PAGES		(DP_PPE_DS_TX_DESC_COUNT / \
 					 ATH12K_MAX_SPT_ENTRIES)
